                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "25ac28a1-0021-48f0-8d5b-cb61fa0e5641",
                        "source_entry_id": "eb754222-226d-3fc7-89c0-4389142178af",
                        "source_sense_id": "12f79779-7693-3b36-bdc0-3298f79da2c2",
                        "target_lang_word": "beguine",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "beguine",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c8a82a27-fd41-3a33-997a-055f4af21e69",
                                        "entry_id": "49525c44-f28e-3402-8327-d75bd77fe21d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A ballroom dance, similar to a slow rumba, originally from French West Indies and popularized abroad largely through the song \\\"Begin the Beguine\\\"; the music for the dance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aecf86fa-e74a-4643-904d-a6346b9c8cdc",
                                                "sense_id": "c8a82a27-fd41-3a33-997a-055f4af21e69",
                                                "text": "When they begin the beguine, / It brings back the sound of music so tender / It brings back the night of tropical splendor, / It brings back a memory ever green."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b693fba4-7142-4ff2-91b7-1bb572063669",
                                                "sense_id": "c8a82a27-fd41-3a33-997a-055f4af21e69",
                                                "text": "1956, Langston Hughes, I Wonder as I Wander, 2003, Arnold Rampersad, Dolan Hubbard (editors), The Collected Works of Langston Hughes, Volume 14: Autobiography, page 69,\nIt was a haunting kind of beguine with a strange sad lyric about slavery and freedom set against insistent drums and voluptuous maracas:"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c7356188-75d7-42b4-9bf7-edb94d9e7bad",
                                                "sense_id": "c8a82a27-fd41-3a33-997a-055f4af21e69",
                                                "text": "He is especially fascinated by the chacha, the percussion instrument that sets the basic rolling rhythmic foundation of the beguine and propels the dancers, writing that “the tempo is set by a shiny tin container filled with pebbles.[…]″"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0854eeb0-cb08-4aa3-b350-bbb6d5babce7",
                        "source_entry_id": "eb754222-226d-3fc7-89c0-4389142178af",
                        "source_sense_id": "12f79779-7693-3b36-bdc0-3298f79da2c2",
                        "target_lang_word": "béguine",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "béguine",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c31095f1-ef8f-3366-8da5-488a5f8b0b4d",
                                        "entry_id": "5c352679-2044-382a-ab14-4551bcbbb5f2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Religieuse qui est soumise aux règles monastiques sans avoir prononcé de vœux."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ab1b24a8-4878-4c5c-90b7-b7a4b7e2743d",
                                                "sense_id": "c31095f1-ef8f-3366-8da5-488a5f8b0b4d",
                                                "text": "Ce mouvement spirituel des béguines, à partir du XIIᵉ siècle, grandit dans les Flandres au nord de la France, et en Allemagne."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "58a6b399-dc5a-4b64-bd1b-08c5c355edb1",
                                                "sense_id": "c31095f1-ef8f-3366-8da5-488a5f8b0b4d",
                                                "text": "« Chez nous, il y a des femmes qu’on nomme béguines. Un certain nombre d’entre elles excellent en arguties et raffolent de nouveautés. Elles lisent la Bible en groupe, sans respect, d’une manière pleine d’audace, et cela en petites assemblées, dans des ateliers et même en pleine rue », s’offusque le moine Guibert de Tournai, lors du concile de Lyon, en 1274."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c62a72b5-ff54-34d5-bec9-0b59b89b5523",
                                        "entry_id": "5c352679-2044-382a-ab14-4551bcbbb5f2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Religieuse d’une communauté des Pays-Bas."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bedd834a-b373-42e3-9703-3c48df77faaa",
                                                "sense_id": "c62a72b5-ff54-34d5-bec9-0b59b89b5523",
                                                "text": "La supérieure des béguines, […], ne put suivre ses compagnes : le lendemain, on la trouvait dans la cave du béguinage, asphyxiée, les bras en croix."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "55a4d060-c9e6-347b-8cea-a27330c6262c",
                                        "entry_id": "5c352679-2044-382a-ab14-4551bcbbb5f2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dévote minutieuse."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated",
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "pejorative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b7b69003-391e-4059-a108-2e68ca4b676c",
                                                "sense_id": "55a4d060-c9e6-347b-8cea-a27330c6262c",
                                                "text": "[…] ; vous les béguines au noir bonnet, vous direz vos patenôtres au lieu de radoter sur l'un et l'autre et en même temps ça vous diminuera votre temps de purgatoire."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2579cf15-998a-392d-b159-e989d5ec5f9e",
                                        "entry_id": "5c352679-2044-382a-ab14-4551bcbbb5f2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Personne qui pratique un mode de vie inspiré de celui des béguinages du Moyen Age."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
